# CTF-10 report input and scan Source proposal, unit 1

This is the first separately held implementation unit from whole-Init audit
4c973f1d. It preserves actual report input and ports General::ScanForReports cache/
request semantics. It does not call the scan from ordinary initialization, create
predefined tables/EIO output, execute a fatal backend, or complete CTF-10 gates.
No target/import/formatter/Cargo/test/scientific result or binary was used.
Root applies only after independent FULL Source review and the current activation
milestone; later units must compose before whole-postlude activation.

## Actual input ownership

The existing RawModel ordered_instances, IDF scanner and compiler default ledger
are reused. Five unnamed report types use Source IdfParser.cc277-301 generated
'<canonical type> <within-type count>' identities. Existing named target parsing,
errors and reconciliation remain literal. The same scanner also retains each
actual report object's physical field count as input-only idf_max_fields metadata;
all type/name/count reconciliation precedes metadata mutation. No second parser,
filename sort, assumed alpha count or Native observation is used.

Direct epJSON retains canonical name-map order. Default staged-IDF loading obtains
the five report order overlays. Original IDD/schema field order, exact missing/
empty/default flags and minimum field count are preserved. Default values are
uppercased as actual getObjectItem does: drawing TRIANGULATE3DFACE, dictionary
REGULAR, EMS NONE. Defaults do not increase Native NumAlphas. The field label for
surface-list warnings remains report_type for epJSON and Report Type for IDF.
The legacy dictionary section count retains actual -1 absent/positive count.

TypedModel retains actual objects through its ordinary compiler path; object
coverage/count now includes these five families. A/B requests remain admitted.
Schema-invalid non-string report alpha or unrepresentable physical count is an
explicit compiler error, not an invented Native successful value. The public
getObjectItem projection is selected for these string-valued non-retaincase fields;
this unit does not claim generic InputProcessor or unused-input ledger completion.

## Literal scan semantics

The real five family passes occur in source order. First scan reads all families,
legacy dictionary state and all options/EMS/global side effects, then clears
GetReportInput. Subsequent scans use retained state without rereading new input.
Existing flags are retained/updated exactly; EMS boolean assignments can reset an
earlier setting, while drawing-family flags accumulate. Options retain within-
family overwrite order. Materials/Constructions and second-alpha NumAlphas>1 stay
distinct. Optional option references change only in their actual query branches.

An unknown surface-list token follows localMap[unknown] -> EMPTY -> the actual
'No ... supplied.' warning plus exact continue argument. No invented Invalid
warning is substituted for the normally unreachable catch(int). Diagnostic
arguments are delivered synchronously to the supplied real caller callback in
source order. This callback interface does not certify warning counters, error
streams, SQLite or external callbacks; their actual backend remains unit 3 work.

The Native Surfaces request dereferences an absent optional ReportKey. Rust returns
MissingSurfacesKey after the genuine first-scan cache changes, without claiming a
Native return/guard/outcome. This boundary does not affect the actual CTF Init call,
which always supplies Constructions/Constructions. Other unsupported request names
follow the actual false result and leave caller options unchanged.

